    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0606" n="504" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">504.418B1/204</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1635</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-16">August 16,
                        1935</date>.<lb/>[Received August 23.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s instruction No. 938 of August 2, 1935, concerning the Roerich Pact
                    and directing the Embassy to inquire orally at the Foreign Office the view with
                    which it is disposed to regard this Convention.</p>
                <p>In reply to an inquiry in the sense of the Department’s instruction, the Foreign
                    Office said that they had been made aware of the Pact and, after considering it,
                    do not feel at present that it is necessary for Great Britain to accede.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray Atherton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
